---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base title="about" description="Electrical engineering student at VJTI. I build robots.">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="ab-head">
      <h1>about</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="ab-grid">
      <img
        class="ab-portrait"
        src={`${base}/assets/operator/portrait.jpg`}
        alt="Kartikey Pathak"
        width="340"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I'm an electrical engineering student at VJTI, Mumbai (2023–2027,
          minor in robotics). I've been building robots since my first year
          and I'm not planning to stop.
        </p>
        <p>
          The thing I chase is the moment a machine starts working. I don't
          give up easily — most of my projects have a long list of versions
          that didn't work before the one you see in the video.
        </p>
        <p>You can genuinely call me at midnight with an idea.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>right now</h2>
      <p>
        Two things. I spent April to August 2026 in Bangalore as the
        electronics and hardware engineer at <a href="https://eyecandyrobotics.com">Eyecandy
        Robotics</a>, drawing the boards inside
        <a href={`${base}/projects/eyecandy/`}>a small legged robot</a> — the
        awkward one was a power board that had to run 17 motors off one
        battery.
      </p>
      <p>
        And my final year project, which is
        <a href={`${base}/projects/axial-flux-motor/`}>a brushless motor with
        no iron in it</a> — the stator is just a circuit board. I simulated it
        before fabricating and found that my own design was giving away 3.3× of
        its torque, which is the most useful thing a simulation has ever told
        me.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>SRA</h2>
      <p>
        Most of my building happens at the Society of Robotics and Automation
        at VJTI. I run workshops there — embedded C, ESP32, sensor fusion —
        and mentor juniors building their first robots. We make and sell
        <a href={`${base}/projects/origins/`}>Wall-E kits</a>; over 200
        students have learned on them so far.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>not robots</h2>
      <p>
        I directed a short film with my friends once — "Plot Se Panga". It
        won first prize across all branches. Turns out directing a film and
        debugging a robot are the same job: many takes, one good one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Also led my branch to a win at Pratibimb, VJTI's cultural fest —
        first time in 26 years. The results came out on my 19th birthday.
      </p>
      <p>
        And there's the <a href={`${base}/projects/robots-for-good/`}>lab
        cat</a>. She has her own robot.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>things I use a lot</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">languages</th><td>C, C++, Python</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">robots</th><td>ROS2, Gazebo, RViz, SLAM, NAV2, URDF, micro-ROS</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">embedded</th><td>ESP32, ESP-IDF, FreeRTOS, ESP-NOW, Raspberry Pi</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">control</th><td>PID, sensor fusion, kinematics</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">vision</th><td>OpenCV, ArUco, CNNs</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">boards</th><td>KiCAD, li-ion charging, BMS, buck converters, motor drivers</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">analysis</th><td>FEMM, magnetostatic FEA</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">making</th><td>OnShape, 3D printing, a soldering iron, an oscilloscope</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <p class="prose">
      Want the formal version? <a href={`${base}/resume.pdf`}>resume (PDF)</a>
      — or <a href={`${base}/plain/`}>everything on one page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .ab-head { padding-top: var(--sp-12); }
    .ab-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 340px 1fr;
      gap: var(--sp-8);
      align-items: start;
      margin-bottom: var(--sp-8);
    }
    .ab-portrait {
      width: 100%;
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    }
    table { max-width: var(--measure); }
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .ab-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .ab-portrait { max-width: 280px; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
